    "title": "Nebraska-Baylor recap, stats and highlights",
    "text": "Updated March 20, 2026, 4:00 p.m. CTNebraska women's basketball (19-13) faced an old Big 12 Conference rival on Friday afternoon. The No. 11 Huskers played the No. 6 Baylor Bears (25-8) in the NCAA First Round on Friday, March 20, in Durham, N.C.Nebraska entered the fourth quarter with a six-point lead over Baylor, but like many times this season, crumbled in the final 10 minutes, resulting in a 67-62 defeat. The Bears outscored the Huskers 26-15 in the fourth, bringing strong pressure and forcing six turnovers and eight fouls. Nebraska finished the game with 22 fouls and 15 turnovers.This led to Baylor going 21-of-29 from the free-throw line and 18 points off turnovers. The Huskers scored 23 points off turnovers, but just 13-of-15 from the line. The Bears also controlled the boards, outrebounding Nebraska 43-33.This negated the Huskers' strong showing from three-point range. Nebraska shot 9-of-21 from beyond the arc, while Baylor finished 4-of-21. The Huskers also hit 20-of-59 from the floor while the Bears totaled 21-of-57.Britt Prince once again led Nebraska in scoring, dropping 27 points after going 8-of-19 in total, 3-of-7 from three-point range and 8-of-8 from the foul line. She finishes the season with 572 total points and brings her career total to 975.Logan Nissley scored 11 points in the loss, shooting 4-of-10 and 3-of-6, respectively. Jessica Petrie rounded out Nebraska's top scorers, finishing the game with 10 points after going 4-of-6, 1-of-2 and 1-of-1. Amiah Hargrove led the Huskers in rebounds, wrangling in 11 to accompany her six points scored on the day.Nebraska ends the season 19-13, reaching its third-straight NCAA Tournament and winning its 10th tournament game on Wednesday against Richmond in the First Four.Final score Final in Durham (Baylor 67-62)Nebraska's season comes to an end. Bears with the lead (Q4 0:57/Baylor 62-59)Baylor is now in front with less than a minute left. Baylor brings the pressure (Q4 4:04/Nebraska 53-52)The Bears crank up the pressure and bring Nebraska's lead down to one.Another three Nebraska up by six (Nebraska 47-41)The Huskers head into the fourth with a firm lead. Huskers stay in front (Q3 4:56/Nebraska 37-35)Nebraska traded blows with the Bears to start the third but remain ahead.Block party Nebraska takes the lead at half (Nebraska 28-27)The Huskers outscored Baylor 17-8 in the second quarter to take the halftime lead.Prince for three Huskers slowly storming back (Q2 4:39/Baylor 23-18)Nebraska cuts the deficit to five halfway through the second.Nebraska striking from afar Baylor ahead through one (Baylor 19-11)Nebraska brings the deficit back to single digits to end the first. Timeout Nebraska (Q1 1:23/Baylor 19-8)The Bears go on another run to put the Huskers in an 11-point deficit. Huskers battling (Q1 4:39/Baylor 9-8)After Baylor opened the game with a 7-0 run, Nebraska responded with an 8-2 surge. Starting fiveHere's how to watch the Nebraska-Baylor basketball game today, including time, TV schedule, and streaming information:What channel is Nebraska-Baylor basketball on today?TV Channel: ESPNLivestream:ESPN+ (subscriber only)Nebraska-Baylor basketball can be seen on ESPN in the first round of the NCAA Tournament. Jenn Hildrith and Kelly Gramlich will call the game courtside from Cameron Indoor Arena. Streaming options for the game include ESPN+.Nebraska-Baylor basketball time todayDate: Friday, March 20Start time: 1 p.m. CTThe Nebraska-Baylor basketball game starts at 1 p.m. CT from Cameron Indoor Stadium in Durham, NC.We occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, and this doesn’t influence our coverage.Contact/Follow us @CornhuskersWire on X (formerly Twitter) and like our page on Facebook to follow ongoing coverage of Nebraska news, notes and opinions.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.We occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, though, and this doesn’t influence our coverage.",
